%T A401394 5004411779425,208135170072169,9402098432123374
%N A401394 Number of labeled graphs on n vertices that are both chordal and claw-free.
%C A401394 Graphs are finite simple graphs with vertex set {1,...,n}. A graph is chordal if it has no induced cycle of length at least 4, and claw-free if it has no induced subgraph isomorphic to K_{1,3}. The term a(0)=1 counts the empty graph.
%C A401394 Terms through n=7 were independently checked by exhaustive Rust enumeration of all 2^binomial(n,2) labeled graphs. Terms through n=14 were obtained by generating the nonisomorphic chordal claw-free graphs with nauty 2.8.8, using geng -TF, and weighting each isomorphism class G by n!/|Aut(G)|.
%D A401394 R. Faudree, E. Flandrin and Z. Ryjáček, Claw-free graphs—A survey, Discrete Mathematics 164 (1997), 87-147.
%D A401394 B. D. McKay and A. Piperno, Practical Graph Isomorphism, II, Journal of Symbolic Computation 60 (2014), 94-112.
%D A401394 N. C. Wormald, Counting labelled chordal graphs, Graphs and Combinatorics 1 (1985), 193-200.
%H A401394 B. D. McKay and A. Piperno, <a href="https://pallini.di.uniroma1.it/">nauty and Traces</a>.
%H A401394 B. D. McKay, <a href="https://users.cecs.anu.edu.au/~bdm/nauty/nug28.pdf">nauty and Traces User's Guide</a>.
%F A401394 a(n) = Sum_G n!/|Aut(G)|, where the sum is over the isomorphism classes G of chordal claw-free graphs on n vertices.
%e A401394 a(4)=57. There are 2^binomial(4,2)=64 labeled graphs on four vertices. Exactly 3 are isomorphic to C_4 and hence are not chordal, and exactly 4 are isomorphic to K_{1,3} and hence are not claw-free. These two sets are disjoint, so a(4)=64-3-4=57.
%Y A401394 Cf. A058862 (labeled chordal graphs), A007134 (connected labeled chordal graphs), A086991 (unlabeled claw-free graphs), and A022562 (connected unlabeled claw-free graphs).
%K A401394 nonn,more,new
